   <title><![CDATA[Ep. 142: The Age of Feeling with Dr. Robert George [The Outstanding Podcast]]]></title>
   <link/>
   <description><![CDATA[<p class="encore-text encore-text-body-medium" data-encore-id="text" data-slate-node="element"><span data-slate-node="text"><span class="sc-fJvzOn lOEQV" data-slate-leaf="true">Host Joseph Backholm is joined by Dr. Robert George, a professor at Princeton University, for a conversation addressing the pressing issues of this generation. First and foremost, Christians are called to protect the unborn. Professor George emphasizes and unpacks how the Republican party has shifted from this narrative and how the Democratic party is not the party of love and compassion, but one of harm to women, immigrants, and Americans. He also gives his thoughts on immigration reform, how higher education impacts culture and the age of feeling.</span></span></p>
